{
  "quest.466E6370698523ED.quest_subtitle": "It's basically a fancy trash can.",
  "quest.7B24F9613AF8F7E1.title": "&bFlares",
  "quest.6040C9A591AB15B1.title": "&bThe Aluminum Wrench",
  "quest.7B24F9613AF8F7E1.quest_subtitle": "Pretty lights go brrr",
  "quest.7B24F9613AF8F7E1.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFlare Rod&r places Flares, small glowing orbs that give off full-strength light.",
    "",
    "Right-click a block to put a Flare in the space next to it. Each Flare costs 5 FE, taken from any charged energy item in your inventory, because the rod has no battery of its own.",
    "",
    "Flares have no hitbox to bump into, can sit underwater and break with a single hit. Breaking one drops nothing, so place a new one rather than trying to pick it up.",
  ],
  "quest.593E47320A36238A.quest_desc": [
    "Despite the name, the &aLight Field&r gives off no light. It stops mobs spawning in a cube 49 blocks across, centered on itself.",
    "",
    "Natural spawns, patrols, phantoms, monster spawners and wandering traders are all blocked inside it. Breeding, spawn eggs, buckets and Trial Spawners still work.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: it stops your own mob spawners too, so keep it out of range of a spawner farm.",
  ],
  "quest.77CD6178BCE6BA74.title": "&bBuilding a Tank",
  "quest.77CD6178BCE6BA74.quest_desc": [
    "A &aValve&r turns a hollow box into a XyCraft fluid tank. Each block of empty space inside holds 8,000 mB, so the 9x9x9 tank pictured here holds 2,744 buckets.",
    "",
    "Build the box first, then right-click the Valve with a wrench to form the tank:",
    "- Size: up to 13 blocks along each side, counting the walls.",
    "- Edges: any full block without a block entity, except glass and loose blocks such as dirt, sand, gravel, wool and leaves.",
    "- Faces: the same blocks as the edges, plus glass. The Valve has to sit in a face, not on an edge.",
    "- Inside: empty air. XyCraft lamps and Flares are allowed.",
    "",
    "Pipe fluid in and out through the Valve. A comparator next to it reads how full the tank is.",
  ],
  "quest.593E47320A36238A.title": "&bThe Light Field",
  "quest.014788EE0C2123E3.title": "&bThe Hydro Pump",
  "quest.4641683810274034.title": "&bThe Buffer",
  "quest.050F04E7BE95E0A1.quest_desc": [
    "Flares come in the 16 dye colors, plus XyCraft's own blue.",
    "",
    "Hold a dye in your offhand while you place Flares with the rod in your main hand, and every Flare comes out in that color.",
    "",
    "[\"To set a default color instead, hold the dye in your other hand, hold \", {\"keybind\": \"key.xycraft_core.modifier_key\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Left Control\"}}, \" and right-click the air with the rod. The tip of the rod changes to show your color, and new Flares use it until you change it.\"]",
    "",
    "To recolor a Flare that's already placed, right-click it with a dye in your main hand. The dye isn't used up.",
  ],
  "quest.6040C9A591AB15B1.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAluminum Wrench&r is XyCraft's primary tool, and it handles every XyCraft machine in this chapter.",
    "",
    "Right-click a XyCraft machine with it to rotate the machine. Mining a XyCraft machine with the wrench breaks it at once and puts it straight into your inventory.",
    "",
    "The wrench also forms tanks, links Flares, and works on many other mods.",
  ],
  "quest.466E6370698523ED.quest_desc": [
    "The &aVoid Container&r deletes whatever it is given, which makes it the way to get rid of overflow.",
    "",
    "Place it against a block. Every 5 ticks it pulls up to 8 items, 1,000 mB of fluid and 100 FE out of that block and deletes them. Anything piped into it is deleted as well.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: whatever goes in is gone for good. It leaves AE2 and Refined Storage drives alone, but on a storage chest it deletes 32 items a second.",
  ],
  "quest.466E6370698523ED.title": "&cThe Void Container",
  "quest.050F04E7BE95E0A1.title": "&dColoring Flares",
  "quest.014788EE0C2123E3.quest_desc": [
    "The &aHydro Pump&r is an endless water source that doesn't need an infinite-source pool built around it.",
    "",
    "Place it against the block you want filled, such as a tank or a machine. Every 5 ticks it pushes 100 mB of water into that block, or 1,000 mB if the pump is waterlogged.",
    "",
    "The block it sits on can also pull water out of it as fast as it likes, so a machine that draws water from it never runs dry.",
  ],
  "quest.2C6E51C798A67EFB.quest_desc": [
    "A &aProxy&r lets you reach a block from somewhere else.",
    "",
    "Place it against a block, and every side of the Proxy acts as the face it was placed on, for items, fluids and energy. A straight line of up to 5 Proxies facing the same way all reach the same block, so you can bring a machine's input out from behind a wall.",
    "",
  ],
  "quest.5B36590EADA598D2.quest_desc": [
    "Pulling resources out of the world around it is the &aExtractor&r's job, and it doesn't need power.",
    "",
    "Place it against a target block and set up what the recipe asks for around that block. The simplest is cobblestone with water and lava next to it, which gives a cobblestone every 30 ticks. JEI lists every Extractor recipe, including the ones that need a catalyst block nearby.",
    "",
    "Output goes out the back of the Extractor, so put a chest or a pipe behind it. A redstone signal pauses it.",
  ],
  "quest.5F9CA56A981D5BF6.title": "&dLinking Flares",
  "quest.2C6E51C798A67EFB.title": "&bThe Proxy",
  "quest.5B36590EADA598D2.title": "&bThe Extractor",
  "quest.5F9CA56A981D5BF6.quest_desc": [
    "Linked Flares are joined by a beam of light that fades from one Flare's color to the other's. The beams are purely decoration.",
    "",
    "With a wrench in hand, right-click one Flare, then right-click another within 12 blocks. Right-click a linked pair again to unlink them.",
    "",
    "[\"Hold \", {\"keybind\": \"key.xycraft_core.modifier_key\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Left Control\"}}, \" on the second click to keep that Flare selected, then click the next one to chain them. Each Flare takes up to 64 links.\"]",
    "",
    "&7&oAny wrench works, and so does a plain stick.&r",
  ],
  "quest.4641683810274034.quest_desc": [
    "A &aBuffer&r gives a machine line 15 slots of holding space.",
    "",
    "Each side of the Buffer reaches its own group of 3 slots, and the front reaches all 15. Pipe a different input into each side to keep them apart, then pull everything out of the front.",
    "",
    "Rotate it with the wrench to choose which face is the front.",
  ],
}